		<title>One Stroke Painting With Donna Dewberry</title>
		<desc lang="en">Painting can sometimes be a frustrating hobby, which is why art classes and television tutorials are pretty popular with today's Michelangelos-in-training. Self-taught artist Donna Dewberry makes things look easy in this instructional series, as she demonstrates how two colors of paint on a brush, along with a few short strokes, can instantly give birth to realistic floral designs. Dewberry also shows how to paint glassware, metal objects and wooden picture frames, all using the innovative technique she developed. With a little practice, viewers will be proudly creating their own cabbage roses and tulips in no time.</desc>
